      "comment_id": "NIST-2021-0007-0075",
      "citation_sentence": "Chairman Papuna Ugrekhelidze outlined three reasons why Georgia was seeking out blockchain as a solution to land registry issues. He states \"first, [blockchain] will add security to the data (property registration) so the data cannot be corrupted. Second, by powering the registry with the blockchain, public auditors will also be able to make real-time audits. So, the auditor will audit the registry not once per year, but every 10 minutes (for example). Third, it will reduce the friction in registration and the cost of property rights registration, because people could do this in the future using their smart phones.\"28",
      "citation_link": null,
      "citation_footnote_text": null,
      "citation_reference_text": "28",
      "unmatched_citation_reference_text": null,
      "cited_source_catagory": "unclassified",
